==Strategy==
While that Dark Catseye might look tempting, Baki's Gauntlet stage makes you work for it. None of the enemies here have any real pushing power, only serving as meatshields for the main threat, Baki himself. With his high health, extreme DPS, and his range, it's going to be a pain to connect any kind of hits onto him. And don't even think about using Talented Awakened Bahamut here given Baki's Explosion Immunity. Your win condition is killing both One Horns: once that's done, you have a clear path to get to Baki.

The best way to do this stage is with [[Cyberpunk Cat]]: while Baki himself is Slow Immune, controlling the supporting peons is a major assistance here. Cyberpunk also serves as a way to chip down Baki's health during the cleanup phase. Build part of your lineup around nuking One Horn as fast as possible, using units like [[Manic Island Cat]], [[Can Can Cat]] and [[Courier Cat]]. Given One Horn's ridiculous health, it's not even that bad of an idea to try more experimental options like [[Luxury Bath Cat]] and [[Elemental Duelist Cat]] here.

